#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bd-docs-only -- decide, fail-closed, whether one candidate can take the
docs-only lane.

OPERATOR RULING 2026-08-31, register row 530. v3.66.1380 changed 65 register
rows and three documents and not one byte under bulk_downloader/, templates or
frontend -- and still consumed a version number, a duplicated version literal,
a CHANGELOG entry, a regeneration, a 14-minute bd-verify-cut, a 6-minute
exact-head CI and a fleet deploy that stops and restarts BD on every serving
host.  It happened again on 2026-09-02: cuts 1447 and 1449 were each two
files, project-knowledge/IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG.md and the manifest that hashes
it, and each paid the same lane and the same five-host deploy.

THE RISK IS THE DEFINITION, NOT THE SAVING. The row says it in its own words:
"a lane that decides for itself what counts as runtime is a lane a product
change can be smuggled through, and getting that denominator wrong is far
worse than the tax it avoids."  So this tool is written as a SAFETY BOUNDARY.

HOW IT IS SAFE, stated as the one property that matters
-------------------------------------------------------
The ALLOW set is small, positively derived, and gated. The DENY set is
everything else.  A path is permitted only when it is proven to be a member of
one of exactly three derived populations:

  1. the tracked Markdown documentation corpus -- the SAME corpus the doc-truth
     and freshness gates judge, obtained from the one rule in
     bdtools_sec.markdown_corpus_from_listing, never a second copy of it;
  2. the release trio, and only when a byte-exact proof shows the head blobs
     differ from base by the version literal alone (that proof is
     bd-band-transfer-key's, reused, not reimplemented);
  3. a tracked output of the regeneration chain, and only when re-running THAT
     generator in a disposable exact-head worktree reproduces the candidate's
     bytes exactly.

Everything else is RUNTIME-AFFECTING.  A path this tool has never heard of is
runtime-affecting.  A new top-level directory is runtime-affecting.  A
measurement that cannot be taken is UNKNOWN (exit 2), which A2 says is a
failing third state and never permission.

The named refusal REASONS are diagnostics on top of that boundary, not the
boundary itself.  A7 forbids collapsing distinct failures into one message --
"repair the service, or find the right password" lead to opposite actions --
so each category answers with its own reason code and its own derived
population.  If a diagnostic population cannot be derived the path still
refuses; it refuses as OUTSIDE-DOC-CORPUS instead of by name.  Losing a
diagnostic can never turn a refusal into permission.

WHERE EVERY POPULATION COMES FROM (nothing here is a typed path list)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
  product source     the directory holding the `__version__` authority --
                     the same file A6 names as edit 1 of the release trio,
                     located by content, not by name.
  templates          the folder token in the application's own
                     Flask(..., template_folder=...) call, resolved both under
                     the package root and as a top-level directory, because the
                     app reads reviewed site templates from the second one.
  frontend           the directory holding the tracked `package.json` that is
                     not under the test root -- the SPA whose build deploy.sh
                     rebuilds.
  tests              the directory holding `conftest.py`; that is what defines
                     a pytest population when no ini file does.
  gate or CI         `.github`, plus the top-level component of every argv path
                     in bd-regen-order's CHAIN.  That derivation is why this
                     file cannot be edited through its own lane: bd-docs-only
                     lives in toolchain/, which the chain names.
  deploy or install  the top-level component of the tracked `deploy.sh` A6
                     calls the sanctioned deploy path.
  generated          bd-regen-order's REQUIRED_CHAIN_LABELS x
                     TRACKED_OUTPUTS_BY_LABEL, read by AST at the BASE commit,
                     exactly as bd-band-transfer-key reads them.
  declared           tools/decomp/import_graph_baseline.json, the reviewed
                     import-edge declaration -- a statement about the runtime
                     import surface, so never docs-only.

Populations are derived at BASE, deliberately.  A7's rule about not deriving an
expected set from the artifact under test applies to a classifier too: a
candidate that edits an authority must not get to redefine the population that
judges it.  It cannot, twice over -- the authorities all live inside the
gate-or-CI population, so touching one is itself a refusal.

WHAT A DOCS-ONLY VERDICT STILL OWES
-----------------------------------
The lane skips the RELEASE tax.  It never skips the correctness gates.  A
DOCS-ONLY verdict carries a required-gate block with four families -- freshness,
register, doc-truth and gate-shard -- each derived by grepping the tracked test
population for that family's authority, each asserted NONZERO, plus the
bd-band-derive band for the changed paths.  An empty family is UNKNOWN, not a
pass; a gate battery over an empty denominator is the defect this repository
exists to refuse.

Usage:
  bd-docs-only classify --repo DIR --base REF --head REF [--json]
  bd-docs-only census   --repo DIR [--commit REF] [--json]
  bd-docs-only selftest

EXIT IS THE VERDICT:
  0  DOCS-ONLY      -- every changed path is proven inert, gates are nonzero
  1  RUNTIME        -- at least one changed path is runtime-affecting
  2  UNKNOWN        -- a required measurement could not be taken
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import ast
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import pathlib
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import bdtools_sec as sec  # noqa: E402

DOCS_ONLY, RUNTIME, UNKNOWN = 0, 1, 2

# Every refusal a changed path can earn. Distinct codes on purpose: A7's
# collapsed-diagnostic rule. Held as a frozen tuple so the gate can pin the set
# and a silent rename shows up as a missing member rather than as nothing.
REASONS = (
    "RUNTIME-PRODUCT-SOURCE",
    "RUNTIME-TEMPLATE",
    "RUNTIME-FRONTEND",
    "RUNTIME-DEPLOY-OR-INSTALL",
    "EVIDENCE-GATE-OR-CI",
    "EVIDENCE-TEST",
    "EVIDENCE-GENERATED-NOT-AT-FIXPOINT",
    "DECLARED-IMPORT-BASELINE",
    "RELEASE-TRIO-PARTIAL",
    "RELEASE-TRIO-BEYOND-VERSION-SUBSTITUTION",
    "OUTSIDE-DOC-CORPUS",
    "UNSUPPORTED-ENTRY-MODE",
    "ENTRY-MODE-CHANGED",
)

# The four correctness families a docs-only cut still owes, each keyed to the
# AUTHORITY its gates cite. The value is a literal search token, not a test
# path: the member set is derived by searching the tracked test population, so
# a family gains and loses gates as the tree does.
GATE_FAMILY_ANCHORS = {
    "freshness": "bd-freshcheck",
    "doc-truth": "bd-doc-truth",
    "register": "IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG",
    "gate-shard": "ci_gate_shards_cover_every_gate",
}

# The two REGULAR blob modes. Git's others are a symlink (120000) and a
# submodule gitlink (160000): a symlink's bytes are a path, and a gitlink's are
# another repository, so neither can be proven inert by reading Markdown.
#
# 100755 belongs here and its absence was a MEASURED collapsed diagnostic. With
# only 100644 regular, an edit to scripts/deploy.sh and an edit to this very
# file both refused as UNSUPPORTED-ENTRY-MODE -- the right verdict wearing the
# wrong reason, sending a reader to look at file permissions instead of at the
# deploy path or the classifier. A7: name the step that failed.
_REGULAR = {"100644", "100755"}

_VERSION_AUTHORITY = re.compile(rb'(?m)^__version__ = "[^"]+"$')
_TEMPLATE_FOLDER = re.compile(r'template_folder\s*=\s*"([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)"')


class Unmeasurable(RuntimeError):
    """A required measurement could not be taken. UNKNOWN, never permission."""


class Refused(RuntimeError):
    """The candidate is runtime-affecting for a named reason."""

    def __init__(self, reason, detail, paths=()):
        super().__init__("%s: %s" % (reason, detail))
        self.reason = reason
        self.detail = detail
        self.paths = tuple(paths)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------- git ---

def _git(repo, *args, binary=False):
    result = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(repo), *args],
        capture_output=True, text=not binary, check=False, timeout=180,
    )
    if result.returncode != 0:
        err = result.stderr if not binary else result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace")
        raise Unmeasurable("git %s failed: %s" % (" ".join(args), err.strip()))
    return result.stdout


def _commit(repo, ref, label):
    if not ref or ref == "UNKNOWN":
        raise Unmeasurable("UNKNOWN identity: %s" % label)
    resolved = _git(repo, "rev-parse", "--verify", ref + "^{commit}").strip()
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40,64}", resolved):
        raise Unmeasurable("%s does not resolve to exactly one commit" % label)
    return resolved


def _listing(repo, commit):
    raw = _git(repo, "ls-tree", "-r", "--name-only", "-z", commit, binary=True)
    paths = [os.fsdecode(item) for item in raw.split(b"\0") if item]
    if not paths:
        raise Unmeasurable("tracked listing at %s collapsed to zero" % commit[:12])
    return paths


def _blob(repo, commit, path):
    return _git(repo, "show", "%s:%s" % (commit, path), binary=True)


def _grep_paths(repo, commit, pattern, pathspec, fixed=True):
    """Tracked paths at `commit` whose content matches, WITHOUT reading 1554 blobs.

    The first draft asked git for every candidate blob and matched in Python:
    correct, and 95 seconds on the real tree, which is a gate nobody runs before
    a lane. git grep does the same search in the object store in one process.
    A grep that finds nothing is not an error here -- the CALLER decides whether
    an empty result is a zero denominator, because only the caller knows.
    """
    argv = ["grep", "-l", "-z", "-I"]
    if fixed:
        argv.append("-F")
    argv += ["-e", pattern, commit, "--", *pathspec]
    result = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), *argv],
                            capture_output=True, check=False, timeout=300)
    if result.returncode not in (0, 1):
        raise Unmeasurable("git grep failed: %s"
                           % result.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip())
    prefix = (commit + ":").encode("ascii")
    paths = []
    for item in result.stdout.split(b"\0"):
        if not item:
            continue
        if not item.startswith(prefix):
            raise Unmeasurable("git grep returned an unqualified path: %r" % item[:80])
        paths.append(os.fsdecode(item[len(prefix):]))
    return paths


def _raw_delta(repo, base, head):
    """Changed paths with their head file mode, from the NET cut.

    The denominator is merge-base..head the way bd-verify-cut defines it, so a
    product change parked in an earlier branch commit cannot hide behind a tidy
    tip.  --no-renames keeps a rename as delete + add: both halves then face
    their own population instead of one similarity score deciding for them.
    """
    raw = _git(repo, "diff", "--no-ext-diff", "--no-renames", "--raw", "-z",
               base, head, binary=True)
    fields = [os.fsdecode(item) for item in raw.split(b"\0") if item]
    entries = []
    index = 0
    while index < len(fields):
        meta = fields[index]
        if not meta.startswith(":"):
            raise Unmeasurable("unparsable diff --raw record: %r" % meta)
        parts = meta[1:].split()
        if len(parts) < 5:
            raise Unmeasurable("unparsable diff --raw record: %r" % meta)
        old_mode, new_mode, _old_oid, _new_oid, status = parts[:5]
        index += 1
        if index >= len(fields):
            raise Unmeasurable("diff --raw record is missing its path")
        path = fields[index]
        index += 1
        entries.append({"path": path, "old_mode": old_mode,
                        "new_mode": new_mode, "status": status})
    return entries


# ------------------------------------------------------------- populations ---

def _one_top_level(paths, label):
    """The single top-level component shared by an authority's own paths."""
    tops = {pathlib.PurePosixPath(p).parts[0] for p in paths
            if pathlib.PurePosixPath(p).parts}
    if len(tops) != 1:
        raise Unmeasurable("%s resolves to %d top-level roots: %s"
                           % (label, len(tops), sorted(tops)))
    return tops.pop()


def _sole(matches, label):
    if len(matches) != 1:
        raise Unmeasurable("%s authority resolves %d times, expected one: %s"
                           % (label, len(matches), sorted(matches)[:6]))
    return matches[0]


def _literal_assignment(source, name, where):
    tree = ast.parse(source, filename=where)
    found = []
    for node in tree.body:
        if not isinstance(node, (ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign)):
            continue
        targets = node.targets if isinstance(node, ast.Assign) else [node.target]
        if any(isinstance(t, ast.Name) and t.id == name for t in targets):
            found.append(ast.literal_eval(node.value))
    if len(found) != 1:
        raise Unmeasurable("%s has %d %s assignments, expected one"
                           % (where, len(found), name))
    return found[0]


def _chain_authority(repo, commit):
    """bd-regen-order's chain, read by AST at the given commit.

    Same technique as bd-band-transfer-key._derived_outputs, and for the same
    reason: the ordering and the product set are the chain's to state, and a
    consumer that retypes either becomes the second hand-maintained list A8
    warns drifts.
    """
    where = "toolchain/bin/bd-regen-order"
    source = _blob(repo, commit, where).decode("utf-8")
    required = tuple(_literal_assignment(source, "REQUIRED_CHAIN_LABELS", where))
    products = _literal_assignment(source, "TRACKED_OUTPUTS_BY_LABEL", where)
    chain = _literal_assignment(source, "CHAIN", where)
    if not required or len(required) != len(set(required)):
        raise Unmeasurable("regeneration chain labels are empty or duplicated")
    if set(products) != set(required):
        raise Unmeasurable(
            "chain labels disagree with tracked outputs: missing=%r unexpected=%r"
            % (sorted(set(required) - set(products)),
               sorted(set(products) - set(required))))
    argv_by_label = {}
    for entry in chain:
        label, argv = entry[0], tuple(entry[1])
        argv_by_label[label] = argv
    if set(argv_by_label) != set(required):
        raise Unmeasurable("chain argv labels disagree with the required labels")
    outputs = {}
    for label in required:
        for path in products[label]:
            pure = pathlib.PurePosixPath(path)
            if pure.is_absolute() or ".." in pure.parts or not pure.parts:
                raise Unmeasurable("unsafe tracked chain output: %r" % (path,))
            if path in outputs:
                raise Unmeasurable("duplicated tracked chain output: %s" % path)
            outputs[path] = label
    if not outputs:
        raise Unmeasurable("the regeneration chain declares no tracked output")
    return {"labels": required, "outputs": outputs, "argv": argv_by_label}


def derive_populations(repo, commit, listing, chain):
    """Every named population, measured from the tree at `commit`.

    Each entry is (root prefixes, member count). A population that resolves to
    zero members is a derivation that has silently stopped seeing its subject,
    so the census gate asserts every count is nonzero rather than trusting that
    an empty set means "nothing to refuse".
    """
    tracked = set(listing)

    version_authority = _sole(
        [p for p in _grep_paths(repo, commit, '__version__ = "', ("*__init__.py",))
         if p in tracked and _VERSION_AUTHORITY.search(_blob(repo, commit, p))],
        "__version__")
    package_root = _one_top_level([version_authority], "the package root")

    app_source = _sole([p for p in listing
                        if p == "%s/app.py" % package_root], "the Flask app module")
    folders = set(_TEMPLATE_FOLDER.findall(
        _blob(repo, commit, app_source).decode("utf-8", "replace")))
    if len(folders) != 1:
        raise Unmeasurable("the app declares %d template_folder tokens" % len(folders))
    template_token = folders.pop()

    conftest = _sole([p for p in listing
                      if pathlib.PurePosixPath(p).name == "conftest.py"], "conftest.py")
    test_root = _one_top_level([conftest], "the test root")

    manifests = [p for p in listing
                 if pathlib.PurePosixPath(p).name == "package.json"
                 and not p.startswith(test_root + "/")]
    spa_root = _one_top_level([_sole(manifests, "package.json")], "the SPA root")

    deploy = _sole([p for p in listing
                    if pathlib.PurePosixPath(p).name == "deploy.sh"], "deploy.sh")
    deploy_root = _one_top_level([deploy], "the deploy root")

    gate_roots = {".github"}
    for argv in chain["argv"].values():
        for token in argv:
            if "/" in token and not token.startswith("-"):
                gate_roots.add(pathlib.PurePosixPath(token).parts[0])

    template_roots = ("%s/%s/" % (package_root, template_token),
                      "%s/static/" % package_root,
                      "%s/" % template_token)

    populations = [
        ("RUNTIME-TEMPLATE", template_roots),
        ("RUNTIME-FRONTEND", ("%s/" % spa_root,)),
        ("RUNTIME-PRODUCT-SOURCE", ("%s/" % package_root,)),
        ("RUNTIME-DEPLOY-OR-INSTALL", ("%s/" % deploy_root,)),
        ("EVIDENCE-GATE-OR-CI", tuple(sorted("%s/" % r for r in gate_roots))),
        ("EVIDENCE-TEST", ("%s/" % test_root,)),
    ]
    counts = {}
    claimed = set()
    for name, roots in populations:
        members = {p for p in tracked
                   if any(p.startswith(root) for root in roots)} - claimed
        counts[name] = len(members)
        claimed |= members

    current, historical = sec.markdown_corpus_from_listing(listing)
    return {
        "order": populations,
        "counts": counts,
        "doc_corpus": set(current) | set(historical),
        "doc_current": len(current),
        "doc_historical": len(historical),
        "package_root": package_root,
        "template_token": template_token,
        "test_root": test_root,
        "spa_root": spa_root,
        "deploy_root": deploy_root,
        "gate_roots": sorted(gate_roots),
        "tracked": len(tracked),
    }


# ------------------------------------------------------ borrowed authorities --

def _load_transfer_key(repo, commit):
    """Import bd-band-transfer-key from the BASE commit, by file.

    The release-trio proof -- head blobs equal base blobs after substituting the
    version literal back, CHANGELOG prepended and anchored on main's head -- is
    already written, already tested and already the merge lane's authority. A8
    says reuse it; rewriting it here would be a second copy of a proof whose
    whole value is that there is one.
    """
    where = "toolchain/bin/bd-band-transfer-key"
    source = _blob(repo, commit, where)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="bd-docs-only-authority-") as directory:
        module_path = os.path.join(directory, "bd_band_transfer_key.py")
        with open(module_path, "wb") as handle:
            handle.write(source)
        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("_bd_docs_only_transfer", module_path)
        if spec is None or spec.loader is None:
            raise Unmeasurable("the release-trio authority cannot be loaded")
        module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
        sys.modules[spec.name] = module
        try:
            spec.loader.exec_module(module)
        except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- any import failure is UNKNOWN
            raise Unmeasurable("the release-trio authority failed to import: %s" % exc)
    for name in ("TRIO", "_trio_disposition", "_trio_evidence", "TransferRefused"):
        if not hasattr(module, name):
            raise Unmeasurable("the release-trio authority is missing %s" % name)
    return module


def _prove_trio(repo, base, head, authority, changed):
    """ABSENT, or COMPLETE and version-substitution-only. Nothing else."""
    try:
        disposition = authority._trio_disposition(changed)
    except authority.TransferRefused as exc:
        raise Refused("RELEASE-TRIO-PARTIAL", str(exc))
    if disposition == "ABSENT":
        return "ABSENT"
    try:
        authority._trio_evidence(repo, base, head)
    except authority.TransferRefused as exc:
        raise Refused("RELEASE-TRIO-BEYOND-VERSION-SUBSTITUTION", str(exc))
    return "COMPLETE"


def _prove_generated_fixpoint(repo, head, chain, generated):
    """Re-run only the generators whose products changed, and demand the bytes.

    A generated artifact in the delta is not authored, so it cannot be judged by
    reading it -- it is judged by whether the tree still produces it. The run
    happens in a disposable exact-head worktree because a classifier that writes
    into the candidate is a classifier that has changed its own subject.
    """
    if not generated:
        return {}
    labels = []
    for label in chain["labels"]:
        if any(chain["outputs"][path] == label for path in generated):
            labels.append(label)
    proved = {}
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="bd-docs-only-fixpoint-") as directory:
        checkout = os.path.join(directory, "exact-head")
        _git(repo, "worktree", "add", "--quiet", "--detach", checkout, head)
        try:
            python = _python_for(repo, checkout)
            declared = [path for path in chain["outputs"]
                        if chain["outputs"][path] in labels]
            before = {}
            for path in declared:
                full = os.path.join(checkout, path)
                if not os.path.isfile(full):
                    raise Unmeasurable("declared chain output %s is absent from the "
                                       "candidate; the fixpoint is UNKNOWN" % path)
                before[path] = os.stat(full).st_mtime_ns
            for label in labels:
                argv = list(chain["argv"][label])
                run = subprocess.run(
                    [python, *argv] if argv[0].endswith(".py") or _is_python(checkout, argv[0])
                    else argv,
                    cwd=checkout, capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, timeout=900,
                )
                if run.returncode != 0:
                    raise Unmeasurable(
                        "generator %s exited %d: %s"
                        % (label, run.returncode, (run.stderr or run.stdout)[-400:].strip()))
            # A GENERATOR THAT EXITS 0 WITHOUT WRITING would leave a hand-edited
            # artifact looking exactly like a fixpoint: the tree is clean because
            # nothing touched it. So the write itself is proven, not assumed.
            unwritten = []
            for path in declared:
                full = os.path.join(checkout, path)
                if not os.path.isfile(full) or os.stat(full).st_mtime_ns <= before[path]:
                    unwritten.append(path)
            if unwritten:
                raise Unmeasurable(
                    "generator(s) %s exited 0 without rewriting %s, so the fixpoint is "
                    "UNKNOWN rather than proven (a filesystem with coarse timestamps "
                    "reads the same way, and reads as UNKNOWN, never as permission)"
                    % (", ".join(labels), ", ".join(unwritten)))
            dirty = _git(checkout, "status", "--porcelain=v1", "--untracked-files=no")
            drifted = sorted(line[3:] for line in dirty.splitlines() if line.strip())
            if drifted:
                # Name the artifact that FAILED, never every artifact examined.
                # Measured on the real tree: a hand-edited PIN_INDEX.json was
                # reported alongside an innocent STATIC_KB_MANIFEST.json purely
                # because both were in the run, which is the same collapsed
                # diagnostic in a different coat.
                raise Refused(
                    "EVIDENCE-GENERATED-NOT-AT-FIXPOINT",
                    "re-running %s did not reproduce the candidate's bytes"
                    % ", ".join(labels),
                    paths=drifted)
            for path in sorted(generated):
                proved[path] = chain["outputs"][path]
        finally:
            removed = subprocess.run(
                ["git", "-C", str(repo), "worktree", "remove", "--force", "--", checkout],
                capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, timeout=120)
            if removed.returncode != 0:
                raise Unmeasurable("temporary fixpoint worktree cleanup is UNKNOWN")
    return proved


def _python_for(repo, checkout):
    for candidate in (os.path.join(checkout, "venv", "bin", "python"),
                      os.path.join(str(repo), "venv", "bin", "python")):
        if os.path.isfile(candidate) and os.access(candidate, os.X_OK):
            return candidate
    return sys.executable


def _is_python(checkout, relative):
    path = os.path.join(checkout, relative)
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as handle:
            return handle.read(2) == b"#!" and b"python" in handle.readline()
    except OSError:
        return False


# ------------------------------------------------------------ required gates --

def required_gates(repo, commit, listing, test_root):
    """The four families a docs-only cut still owes, derived and nonzero."""
    tests = [p for p in listing
             if p.startswith(test_root + "/")
             and pathlib.PurePosixPath(p).name.startswith("test")
             and p.endswith(".py")]
    if not tests:
        raise Unmeasurable("the tracked test population collapsed to zero")
    known = set(tests)
    families = {}
    for family, anchor in GATE_FAMILY_ANCHORS.items():
        members = sorted(set(_grep_paths(repo, commit, anchor,
                                         ("%s/test*.py" % test_root,))) & known)
        if not members:
            raise Unmeasurable(
                "gate family %r has a ZERO denominator: nothing in the %d tracked "
                "test files cites %s" % (family, len(tests), anchor))
        families[family] = members
    return {"tests_examined": len(tests), "families": families}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- classify ---

def classify(repo, base_ref, head_ref, prove_fixpoint=True):
    repo = pathlib.Path(repo).resolve()
    head = _commit(repo, head_ref, "head")
    base_named = _commit(repo, base_ref, "base")
    merge_base = _git(repo, "merge-base", base_named, head).strip()
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40,64}", merge_base):
        raise Unmeasurable("merge-base(base, head) is UNKNOWN")
    base = merge_base

    entries = _raw_delta(repo, base, head)
    if not entries:
        raise Unmeasurable("the candidate changed-path denominator is ZERO")
    changed = {entry["path"] for entry in entries}

    base_listing = _listing(repo, base)
    head_listing = _listing(repo, head)
    chain = _chain_authority(repo, base)
    populations = derive_populations(repo, base, base_listing, chain)
    corpus = set(sec.markdown_corpus_from_listing(base_listing)[0]) \
        | set(sec.markdown_corpus_from_listing(base_listing)[1]) \
        | set(sec.markdown_corpus_from_listing(head_listing)[0]) \
        | set(sec.markdown_corpus_from_listing(head_listing)[1])

    authority = _load_transfer_key(repo, base)
    trio_paths = set(authority.TRIO)
    declared = authority.DECLARED

    refusals = []
    allowed = {}

    # A non-regular entry is refused before anything reads it: a symlink's bytes
    # are a path, and a mode flip is a permission change, not a document edit.
    for entry in entries:
        modes = {entry["old_mode"], entry["new_mode"]} - {"000000"}
        if not modes <= _REGULAR:
            refusals.append({"path": entry["path"],
                             "reason": "UNSUPPORTED-ENTRY-MODE",
                             "detail": "modes %s -> %s (status %s) are not a regular "
                                       "tracked blob" % (entry["old_mode"],
                                                         entry["new_mode"],
                                                         entry["status"])})
        elif len(modes) > 1:
            # Both regular, but the executable bit moved. That is a permission
            # change, not a document edit, and it gets its own name rather than
            # borrowing the non-regular one.
            refusals.append({"path": entry["path"],
                             "reason": "ENTRY-MODE-CHANGED",
                             "detail": "the tracked mode changed %s -> %s; a permission "
                                       "change is not a document edit"
                                       % (entry["old_mode"], entry["new_mode"])})

    refused_paths = {r["path"] for r in refusals}

    # The release trio first: its pin lives inside the test population, so a
    # membership test would refuse the trio for the wrong reason and the real
    # proof -- version substitution and nothing else -- would never run.
    trio_state = "ABSENT"
    if trio_paths & changed:
        try:
            trio_state = _prove_trio(repo, base, head, authority, changed)
        except Refused as exc:
            refusals.append({"path": ", ".join(sorted(trio_paths & changed)),
                             "reason": exc.reason, "detail": exc.detail})
            refused_paths |= (trio_paths & changed)
        else:
            for path in sorted(trio_paths & changed):
                allowed[path] = "RELEASE-TRIO-VERSION-SUBSTITUTION-ONLY"

    generated = set()
    for path in sorted(changed - refused_paths - set(allowed)):
        if path == declared:
            refusals.append({"path": path, "reason": "DECLARED-IMPORT-BASELINE",
                             "detail": "the reviewed import-edge declaration states the "
                                       "runtime import surface"})
            continue
        if path in chain["outputs"]:
            # BEFORE the population prefixes, deliberately. Two chain outputs
            # live inside a deny root -- tests/source_window_hashes.json under
            # the test root and the generated frontend secret keys under the SPA
            # root -- and a prefix rule would refuse them as a hand-written test
            # or a hand-written component, sending the reader to look for an edit
            # that is not there. A chain output is not authored, so it is judged
            # by whether this tree still PRODUCES it, which is the stronger test:
            # it cannot change at all unless one of its generator's inputs
            # changed, and every such input is itself either refused here or a
            # document.
            generated.add(path)
            continue
        named = None
        for name, roots in populations["order"]:
            if any(path.startswith(root) for root in roots):
                named = name
                break
        if named is not None:
            refusals.append({"path": path, "reason": named,
                             "detail": "member of the derived %s population" % named})
            continue
        if path in corpus:
            allowed[path] = "DOC-CORPUS"
            continue
        refusals.append({
            "path": path, "reason": "OUTSIDE-DOC-CORPUS",
            "detail": "tracked but outside the derived Markdown documentation corpus, "
                      "so nothing proves it inert"})

    fixpoint = {}
    if generated and not refusals:
        if prove_fixpoint:
            try:
                fixpoint = _prove_generated_fixpoint(repo, head, chain, generated)
            except Refused as exc:
                refusals.append({"path": ", ".join(exc.paths or sorted(generated)),
                                 "reason": exc.reason, "detail": exc.detail})
            else:
                for path in sorted(generated):
                    allowed[path] = "REGENERATION-CHAIN-FIXPOINT"
        else:
            raise Unmeasurable(
                "the regeneration fixpoint proof was skipped, so %d generated path(s) "
                "are UNKNOWN" % len(generated))
    deferred = []
    if generated and refusals:
        # The candidate is ALREADY refused, so the fixpoint run buys nothing --
        # but naming these paths with a refusal code they have not earned would
        # be the collapsed diagnostic A7 forbids, and would send a reader to
        # repair a generator that is fine. They are reported as UNPROVEN.
        deferred = sorted(generated)

    verdict = {
        "schema": 1,
        "repo": str(repo),
        "base": base,
        "head": head,
        "changed": sorted(changed),
        "changed_count": len(changed),
        "trio": trio_state,
        "allowed": {path: allowed[path] for path in sorted(allowed)},
        "refusals": sorted(refusals, key=lambda r: (r["reason"], r["path"])),
        "fixpoint_proved": {path: fixpoint[path] for path in sorted(fixpoint)},
        "fixpoint_unproven": deferred,
        "populations": populations["counts"],
        "doc_corpus": len(corpus),
        "roots": {"package": populations["package_root"],
                  "template_token": populations["template_token"],
                  "tests": populations["test_root"],
                  "spa": populations["spa_root"],
                  "deploy": populations["deploy_root"],
                  "gate": populations["gate_roots"]},
    }
    if refusals:
        verdict["verdict"] = "RUNTIME-AFFECTING"
        return RUNTIME, verdict

    if set(allowed) != changed:
        raise Unmeasurable(
            "classification is incomplete: %d changed path(s) reached no disposition"
            % len(changed - set(allowed)))

    gates = required_gates(repo, head, head_listing, populations["test_root"])
    verdict["required_gates"] = {
        "tests_examined": gates["tests_examined"],
        "families": {family: {"count": len(members), "members": members}
                     for family, members in gates["families"].items()},
    }
    verdict["verdict"] = "DOCS-ONLY"
    return DOCS_ONLY, verdict


def census(repo, ref):
    repo = pathlib.Path(repo).resolve()
    commit = _commit(repo, ref, "commit")
    listing = _listing(repo, commit)
    chain = _chain_authority(repo, commit)
    populations = derive_populations(repo, commit, listing, chain)
    authority = _load_transfer_key(repo, commit)
    return {
        "schema": 1,
        "commit": commit,
        "tracked": populations["tracked"],
        "populations": populations["counts"],
        "doc_current": populations["doc_current"],
        "doc_historical": populations["doc_historical"],
        "chain_outputs": sorted(chain["outputs"]),
        "trio": sorted(authority.TRIO),
        "declared": authority.DECLARED,
        "reasons": list(REASONS),
        "roots": {"package": populations["package_root"],
                  "template_token": populations["template_token"],
                  "tests": populations["test_root"],
                  "spa": populations["spa_root"],
                  "deploy": populations["deploy_root"],
                  "gate": populations["gate_roots"]},
    }


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- selftest ---

def _fixture_repo(directory):
    """A miniature tree carrying every authority this tool derives from."""
    root = pathlib.Path(directory)

    def write(rel, text, mode=None):
        path = root / rel
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        path.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
        if mode is not None:
            os.chmod(path, mode)

    write("bulk_downloader/__init__.py", '__version__ = "9.9.1"\n')
    write("bulk_downloader/app.py",
          'def make():\n    return Flask(__name__, template_folder="templates",'
          ' static_folder="static")\n')
    write("bulk_downloader/templates/page.html", "<p>one</p>\n")
    write("bulk_downloader/static/app.css", "body{}\n")
    write("templates/reviewed/site.template.json", '{"a": 1}\n')
    write("frontend/package.json", '{"name": "spa"}\n')
    write("frontend/src/main.ts", "export const x = 1;\n")
    write("tests/conftest.py", "\n")
    write("tests/test_settings_center_slice4.py",
          'from bulk_downloader import __version__\n\n\n'
          'def test_pin():\n    assert __version__ == "9.9.1"\n')
    write("tests/test_other.py", "def test_other():\n    assert True\n")
    # One gate per required family. Their presence is what the POS case proves;
    # a fixture without them is the NEG case below, and it must be UNKNOWN.
    write("tests/test_fresh.py", "# runs bd-freshcheck\ndef test_f():\n    assert True\n")
    write("tests/test_doctruth.py", "# runs bd-doc-truth\ndef test_d():\n    assert True\n")
    write("tests/test_register.py",
          "# reads IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG\ndef test_r():\n    assert True\n")
    write("tests/test_shards.py",
          "# mirrors ci_gate_shards_cover_every_gate\ndef test_s():\n    assert True\n")
    write("scripts/deploy.sh", "#!/bin/sh\necho deploy\n")
    write(".github/workflows/ci.yml", "name: ci\n")
    write("tools/decomp/import_graph_baseline.json", '{"edges": {}, "edge_count": 0}\n')
    write("tools/gen_manifest.py",
          "import hashlib, pathlib, json\n"
          "root = pathlib.Path('.')\n"
          "docs = sorted(p.as_posix() for p in root.glob('project-knowledge/*.md'))\n"
          "payload = {d: hashlib.sha256((root / d).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for d in docs}\n"
          "(root / 'project-knowledge' / 'MANIFEST.json').write_text("
          "json.dumps(payload, indent=1, sort_keys=True) + '\\n')\n")
    write("toolchain/bin/bd-regen-order",
          "REQUIRED_CHAIN_LABELS = (\n    \"MANIFEST\",\n)\n"
          "TRACKED_OUTPUTS_BY_LABEL = {\n"
          "    \"MANIFEST\": (\"project-knowledge/MANIFEST.json\",),\n}\n"
          "CHAIN = [\n    (\"MANIFEST\", [\"tools/gen_manifest.py\"], \"why\"),\n]\n")
    # The REAL release-trio authority, not a stand-in: the fixture must prove
    # this tool's reuse of bd-band-transfer-key, and a stub would prove a stub.
    authority = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "bd-band-transfer-key"
    write("toolchain/bin/bd-band-transfer-key",
          authority.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), mode=0o755)
    write("CHANGELOG.md", "# Changelog\n\n## v9.9.1 - first\n\n- one\n")
    write("CLAUDE.md", "# contract\n")
    write("docs/repo/TOPOLOGY.md", "# topology\n")
    write("project-knowledge/IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG.md", "| 1 | OPEN | a |\n")
    write("project-knowledge/spa_shot.py", "print('shot')\n")
    write("kb/notes.txt", "loose\n")
    return root


def _fixture_git(root, *args, check=True):
    result = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(root), *args],
                            capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, timeout=120)
    if check and result.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError("fixture git %s failed: %s" % (" ".join(args), result.stderr))
    return result


def _fixture_commit(root, message):
    _fixture_git(root, "add", "-A")
    _fixture_git(root, "-c", "user.email=selftest@example.invalid",
                 "-c", "user.name=selftest", "commit", "-q", "-m", message)
    return _fixture_git(root, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()


def _fixture_regen(root):
    subprocess.run([sys.executable, "tools/gen_manifest.py"], cwd=str(root),
                   capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, timeout=120)


def selftest():
    ok = True

    def report(good, line):
        nonlocal ok
        ok = ok and good
        print(("PASS  " if good else "FAIL  ") + line)

    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="bd-docs-only-selftest-") as directory:
        root = _fixture_repo(directory)
        _fixture_git(root, "init", "-q", "-b", "main")
        _fixture_regen(root)
        base = _fixture_commit(root, "base")

        # The census must see every population it claims to judge.
        head_census = census(root, base)
        counts = head_census["populations"]
        report(all(counts[name] > 0 for name in counts),
               "CENSUS: every derived population is NONZERO on the fixture %s" % counts)
        report(head_census["roots"]["package"] == "bulk_downloader"
               and head_census["roots"]["tests"] == "tests"
               and head_census["roots"]["spa"] == "frontend"
               and head_census["roots"]["deploy"] == "scripts"
               and head_census["roots"]["template_token"] == "templates",
               "CENSUS: roots are derived by content, not typed (%s)"
               % head_census["roots"])

        def cut(name, mutate):
            _fixture_git(root, "checkout", "-q", "-b", name, base)
            mutate()
            _fixture_regen(root)
            head = _fixture_commit(root, name)
            _fixture_git(root, "checkout", "-q", "main")
            return head

        def edit_doc():
            (root / "project-knowledge" / "IMPROVEMENT_BACKLOG.md").write_text(
                "| 1 | DONE | a |\n", encoding="utf-8")

        # POSITIVE CONTROL. It must pass, and every adversarial case below is
        # this delta plus exactly one path -- so a refusal names the added path
        # and cannot be laundered by some unrelated earlier condition (A5).
        head = cut("docs", edit_doc)
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        report(rc == DOCS_ONLY and verdict["verdict"] == "DOCS-ONLY",
               "POS: a register + manifest delta is DOCS-ONLY (rc=%d, %s)"
               % (rc, verdict.get("refusals")))
        report(verdict["allowed"].get("project-knowledge/MANIFEST.json")
               == "REGENERATION-CHAIN-FIXPOINT",
               "POS: the regenerated manifest is allowed by FIXPOINT PROOF, not by name")

        adversarial = [
            ("RUNTIME-PRODUCT-SOURCE", "bulk_downloader/db.py", "X = 1\n"),
            ("RUNTIME-TEMPLATE", "bulk_downloader/templates/new.html", "<p>two</p>\n"),
            ("RUNTIME-FRONTEND", "frontend/src/added.ts", "export const y = 2;\n"),
            ("EVIDENCE-GATE-OR-CI", ".github/workflows/extra.yml", "name: extra\n"),
            ("EVIDENCE-TEST", "tests/test_added.py", "def test_added():\n    assert True\n"),
            ("RUNTIME-DEPLOY-OR-INSTALL", "scripts/extra.sh", "#!/bin/sh\n"),
            ("DECLARED-IMPORT-BASELINE", "tools/decomp/import_graph_baseline.json",
             '{"edges": {"a": ["b"]}, "edge_count": 1}\n'),
            ("OUTSIDE-DOC-CORPUS", "project-knowledge/spa_shot.py", "print('changed')\n"),
        ]
        for expected, path, text in adversarial:
            def mutate(path=path, text=text):
                edit_doc()
                target = root / path
                target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                target.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
            head = cut("adv-" + expected.lower(), mutate)
            rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
            reasons = {r["reason"] for r in verdict.get("refusals", [])}
            good = rc == RUNTIME and reasons == {expected}
            report(good, "ADV %-42s -> %s (rc=%d)" % (path, sorted(reasons) or "NONE", rc))

        # The generated artifact that was HAND-EDITED, which is the shape a
        # product change would take if it hid behind "it is only generated".
        def tamper():
            edit_doc()
            _fixture_regen(root)
            manifest = root / "project-knowledge" / "MANIFEST.json"
            manifest.write_text(manifest.read_text().replace("{", "{\n \"smuggled\": 1,", 1),
                                encoding="utf-8")
        _fixture_git(root, "checkout", "-q", "-b", "adv-fixpoint", base)
        tamper()
        head = _fixture_commit(root, "adv-fixpoint")
        _fixture_git(root, "checkout", "-q", "main")
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        reasons = {r["reason"] for r in verdict.get("refusals", [])}
        report(rc == RUNTIME and reasons == {"EVIDENCE-GENERATED-NOT-AT-FIXPOINT"},
               "ADV hand-edited generated artifact -> %s (rc=%d)" % (sorted(reasons), rc))

        # A partial trio and a trio that carries more than its version literal.
        def partial_trio():
            edit_doc()
            (root / "bulk_downloader" / "__init__.py").write_text(
                '__version__ = "9.9.2"\n', encoding="utf-8")
        head = cut("adv-trio-partial", partial_trio)
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        reasons = {r["reason"] for r in verdict.get("refusals", [])}
        report(rc == RUNTIME and "RELEASE-TRIO-PARTIAL" in reasons,
               "ADV a partial release trio -> %s (rc=%d)" % (sorted(reasons), rc))

        def full_trio(extra=""):
            def mutate():
                edit_doc()
                (root / "bulk_downloader" / "__init__.py").write_text(
                    '__version__ = "9.9.2"\n' + extra, encoding="utf-8")
                (root / "tests" / "test_settings_center_slice4.py").write_text(
                    'from bulk_downloader import __version__\n\n\n'
                    'def test_pin():\n    assert __version__ == "9.9.2"\n', encoding="utf-8")
                (root / "CHANGELOG.md").write_text(
                    "# Changelog\n\n## v9.9.2 - second\n\n- two\n\n## v9.9.1 - first\n\n- one\n",
                    encoding="utf-8")
            return mutate

        head = cut("trio-clean", full_trio())
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        report(rc == DOCS_ONLY and verdict["trio"] == "COMPLETE",
               "POS: a version-substitution-only trio stays DOCS-ONLY (rc=%d, %s)"
               % (rc, verdict.get("refusals")))

        head = cut("trio-smuggled", full_trio("SMUGGLED = True\n"))
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        reasons = {r["reason"] for r in verdict.get("refusals", [])}
        report(rc == RUNTIME and reasons == {"RELEASE-TRIO-BEYOND-VERSION-SUBSTITUTION"},
               "ADV a trio carrying product source -> %s (rc=%d)" % (sorted(reasons), rc))

        # A symlink is a path, not a document.
        def symlink():
            edit_doc()
            os.symlink("../bulk_downloader/app.py", str(root / "docs" / "LINK.md"))
        head = cut("adv-symlink", symlink)
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        reasons = {r["reason"] for r in verdict.get("refusals", [])}
        report(rc == RUNTIME and reasons == {"UNSUPPORTED-ENTRY-MODE"},
               "ADV a symlink named *.md -> %s (rc=%d)" % (sorted(reasons), rc))

        def chmod_doc():
            edit_doc()
            os.chmod(str(root / "CLAUDE.md"), 0o755)
        head = cut("adv-mode", chmod_doc)
        rc, verdict = classify(root, base, head)
        reasons = {r["reason"] for r in verdict.get("refusals", [])}
        report(rc == RUNTIME and reasons == {"ENTRY-MODE-CHANGED"},
               "ADV a document that became executable -> %s (rc=%d)" % (sorted(reasons), rc))

        # An empty delta is UNKNOWN, never docs-only.
        try:
            classify(root, base, base)
        except Unmeasurable as exc:
            report("ZERO" in str(exc), "NEG: an empty delta is UNKNOWN (%s)" % exc)
        else:
            report(False, "NEG: an empty delta returned a verdict")

    print("SELFTEST PASS" if ok else "SELFTEST FAIL")
    return 0 if ok else 1


# -------------------------------------------------------------------- main ---

def _emit(payload, as_json):
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True, indent=1))
        return
    if "verdict" in payload:
        print("%s  base=%s head=%s over %d changed path(s)"
              % (payload["verdict"], payload["base"][:12], payload["head"][:12],
                 payload["changed_count"]))
        for path, why in payload["allowed"].items():
            print("  allow   %-58s %s" % (path, why))
        for row in payload["refusals"]:
            print("  REFUSE  %-58s %s" % (row["path"], row["reason"]))
            print("          %s" % row["detail"])
        gates = payload.get("required_gates")
        if gates:
            print("  required gates over %d tracked test file(s):"
                  % gates["tests_examined"])
            for family, detail in sorted(gates["families"].items()):
                print("    %-12s %d gate(s)" % (family, detail["count"]))
        return
    print("census of %s over %d tracked path(s)" % (payload["commit"][:12], payload["tracked"]))
    for name, count in payload["populations"].items():
        print("  %-34s %d" % (name, count))
    print("  %-34s %d current, %d historical"
          % ("DOC-CORPUS", payload["doc_current"], payload["doc_historical"]))


def main(argv=None):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="bd-docs-only")
    # The house convention is a --selftest FLAG, and bd-tool-lint enforces it.
    # It is kept alongside the `selftest` subcommand rather than replacing it so
    # neither spelling becomes the one a future caller guesses wrong.
    parser.add_argument("--selftest", action="store_true",
                        help="run the built-in battery and exit")
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command")
    c = sub.add_parser("classify")
    c.add_argument("--repo", required=True)
    c.add_argument("--base", required=True)
    c.add_argument("--head", required=True)
    c.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    n = sub.add_parser("census")
    n.add_argument("--repo", required=True)
    n.add_argument("--commit", default="HEAD")
    n.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sub.add_parser("selftest")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)

    if args.selftest or args.command == "selftest":
        return selftest()
    if not args.command:
        parser.error("a subcommand is required: classify, census or selftest")
    try:
        if args.command == "classify":
            rc, payload = classify(args.repo, args.base, args.head)
        else:
            rc, payload = DOCS_ONLY, census(args.repo, args.commit)
    except Unmeasurable as exc:
        print("UNKNOWN, not permission: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
        return UNKNOWN
    except (OSError, SyntaxError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        print("UNKNOWN, not permission: %s" % exc, file=sys.stderr)
        return UNKNOWN
    _emit(payload, args.json)
    return rc


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
